course: dictionary
lesson: 15477
title: Stratum and strata
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stratum is one layer. It is a science word, and it is often used for layers of rock or soil. Strata is the plural, meaning more than one layer. «The cliff showed three strata of rock, one on top of another.» Three layers, so strata is the plural of stratum.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «The lowest stratum of the cliff was the oldest», the words lowest and oldest tell you that the bottom layer formed first. Scientists use this idea to date fossils, because lower layers are usually older.
explain: Stratum has a second meaning too. In «The warm stratum of air sat above the cold air», it means a layer of air. People can also be a stratum: «The upper stratum of society had most of the money» means the group at the top level of wealth or power.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a simpler word. Does «The lowest layer of the cliff was the oldest» still make sense? Yes, so layer is a good meaning for stratum. For the people meaning, try «the upper group of society» to check.
fact: Stratum means one layer, and strata means more than one layer.
fact: In science, a stratum is a layer of rock or soil lying on top of another.
fact: Strata are the layers you can see in cliffs and canyons, such as the Grand Canyon.
fact: Lower strata are usually older, which is why they help scientists date fossils.
fact: Stratum can also mean a level or class of people in a society, as in «a social stratum».
exercise: «The cliff showed three strata of rock.» What does strata mean? | Stones that have broken off | *Layers | Long cracks in a wall | Holes in the ground
exercise: In «The lowest stratum of the cliff was the oldest», which layer is probably the oldest? | The layer with the most plants | The top layer | The middle layer, always | *The lowest layer
exercise: In «The upper stratum of society had most of the money», what does stratum mean? | A kind of soup | *A group at one level of wealth or power | A type of cloud | A small house on a hill
test: Stratum is one layer. What is the plural? | Stratu | *Strata | Stratas | Stratos
test: In science, a stratum is a layer of rock or soil. Which description fits best? | *Something that sits on top of another layer of rock or soil | A tool for digging holes | A bird's nest high in a tree | A kind of storm at sea
exam: The scientist said, «The lower strata are usually older.» What does this tell us? | *The bottom layers are often the oldest | The top layers are always the oldest | Scientists cannot date rocks at all | Strata are always made of water
